# Competition inputs are never committed: they are login-gated and licence-restricted.
# They are resolved from the sandbox bridge as symlinks (see data_manifest.json for pins).
# The rule is the whole directory: data/ also holds the 2.2 GB read-only sibling mirror used by the
# uniqueness screen (data/registry, data/registry_flat) and the assembled float32 fields (data/_bridge).
# None of it is a deliverable; everything here is regenerated by scripts/get_inputs.sh + scripts/build_fields.py.
data/
# Rasters and model outputs are kept out of Git (use external storage if they must be shared).
*.tif
*.tiff
*.npy
*.npz
*.zip
# The lane's own published deliverables are hosted on Pages: predictions and receipts, never organizer data.
!docs/downloads/*.tif
!docs/downloads/*.zip
!evidence/*.npz
!evidence/*.json.gz
# Python / tooling
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
*.pyc
_pr_body.md
_venv.log
data/_screen.log
data/_lane_gate.log
# --- competition inputs: never committed (login-gated, licence-restricted) ---
# Run A (this branch) reassembles them from the sha256-pinned bridge (data/README.md,
# scripts/assemble_data_bridge.py); run B resolves them from the sandbox bridge as
# recorded in data_manifest.json / registry/input_pins.json.
data/*.tif
data/bridge/*.part-*
data/cache/
data/reconstructed/
data/raw/
data/interim/
data/external/
data/grid/

# --- rasters, model outputs and archives stay out of Git ---

# --- the published deliverables are the exception: they are hosted on Pages ---
!data/bridge/*.tif

# --- receipts and derived tables are text/committed audit trail ---

# --- python / tooling ---
venv/

# holdout arm rasters are intermediates (regenerate with scripts/holdout_corrections.py)
data/cache/holdout_arms/
